# Deny everything, then allow back only what is meant to be shared. Claude Code
# writes caches, transcripts, plugin payloads and machine state into this
# directory, so listing what to exclude loses the race with the next release.
# Anything that appears here is ignored until a line below names it.
*

!.gitignore

# Shared instructions, and the statusline script with its tests.
!/CLAUDE.md
!/README.md
!/statusline-command.sh
!/statusline-command.test.sh

# Skills, named one directory at a time. The two lines above the list make the
# directories traversable; without them every negation below is dead, because
# git will not descend into a directory that is still excluded. A skill is
# shared only once it is listed here, so a new one is never swept in by
# accident — add a line when you mean to publish it.
#
# Do not replace this list with a broad negation such as `!/skills/**`. That
# publishes every skill in the directory, including any deliberately left off
# the list, and no local ignore file can prevent it — this file sits above
# .git/info/exclude in git's order of precedence. Measured: with `!/skills/**`
# here, an unlisted skill's files staged, exactly as they did with
# .git/info/exclude emptied out.
!/skills/
!/skills/**/
!/skills/clear-task/**
!/skills/create-task-skill/**
!/skills/design-gap-task/**
!/skills/elixir-development/**
!/skills/git-commit/**
!/skills/grill-me/**
!/skills/pr-create-task/**
!/skills/pr-feedback-task/**
!/skills/pr-respond-task/**
!/skills/quick-review/**
!/skills/security-review/**
!/skills/session-loop/**
!/skills/systematize/**
!/skills/tdd-cycle/**
!/skills/writing-code/**

# OS and editor droppings, anywhere. Redundant against the deny-all above, kept
# because these are the ones that get re-allowed by accident.
.DS_Store
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.orig
*.backup*
__pycache__/
*.pyc
